Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 17:15:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] drm: retain the tethered warm boot state

A tethered kernel inherits initialized hardware rather than power-on
state. Retain the board-selected warm handoff state so probe and
shutdown do not discard resources needed by the incoming kernel.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/adbe/adbe_drv.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/adbe/adbe_drv.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/adbe/adbe_drv.c
index 2508e6531..7ed2de3d7 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/adbe/adbe_drv.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/adbe/adbe_drv.c
@@ -1065,6 +1065,9 @@ static void adbe_shutdown(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	struct adbe *adbe = platform_get_drvdata(pdev);
 
 	drm_atomic_helper_shutdown(&adbe->drm);
+	timer_delete_sync(&adbe->flip_timer);
+	/* release9: restore the boot buffer even if the CRTC was never enabled. */
+	adbe_park(adbe);
 	writel(adbe->saved_inten, adbe->regs + ADP_INTEN);
 }
 
